It seems harder, than I thought. ISO I produced is 750 MB, whereas 
original is ~690 MB. It won't fit onto ordinary CD. My steps were :

1. Copy original CD contents :

cd original-cd-root/
tar cf - . | tar xf - -C /new/cd/root/

2. Copy / make aboot files, as far as I understand manuals :

# cp /boot/bootlx /new/cd/root/
# vi /new/cd/root/etc/aboot.conf
# cat /new/cd/root/etc/aboot.conf
0:vmunix


3. Make the ISO image :

# cd /new/cd/root/
# mkisofs -r -o ../new.iso ./

4. Make the image bootable with aboot utility :

# isomarkboot ./new.iso bootlx
iso: Max size:385278   Log zone size:2048
iso: First datazone:35   Root inode number 71680
isomarkboot: bootlx is at offset 3913728 and is 88064 bytes long

Anyone sees obvious errors ?

I have a doubt if the aboot.conf file is correct - I think vmunix should 
be instructed where to look for initrd, where is its root and so on. But 
I don't know the parameters.

Tommorrow I'll get 800 MB CDRs and give it a try.

